 "comment": "Palutena's parts shown on demand (A10, scripts/p6/look_parts.py): each a model-part variant of an existing row drawing that row's list plus cut-out cards, two-sided. Corners are in the look's rest model space (y up, she faces +z; the battle camera sees her x axis as depth, so the cards lie across y and z). The wings (forward and down smash: SetModelPartID joint 6 part 1) are the kit's wing image (godwing, its full feathered wing, the island above it cleared), one card a side sweeping up and back from her shoulder blades. The halo (up air, the down taunt, the victory and select poses: joint 12 part 2) is an authored gold ring above her head, two crossed cards: one faces the battle camera, the other the select and Results cameras, which see her from the front. The light pillar (up smash: joint 5, the hips row, variants 1-5 shown in turn by its script; owner playtest 2026-10-14: a strong light burst of several sprites, 1.25x taller, always in front of her) is an authored column of light ahead of her where the up smash's hitboxes stand (TopN z 260, y 0-1560): one atlas (authored:pillar_burst: core, ray glow, star flare, bloom, sparks), its cards facing the battle camera, each card twice, at either side of her in depth, so the one toward the camera always draws in front of her whichever way she faces; ignite (a thin core and a bloom at its foot), burst (glow, core, flare, sparks), sustain (the glow mirrored, sparks higher), fade, thin.",
